# Compile-time errors

.row gap:{1cm} cross:{start} 
    .container width:{50%} textalignment:{start}
        ## Mismatching types

        Statically typed languages require that the type of a variable is known at compile time. This can lead to errors if the types do not match.

        Can you explain why the highlighted code will not compile?

    .container width:{50%}
        .code lang:{cpp} focus:{16..16} 
            #include <iostream>
            #include <string>

            double compute_average(int a, int b) {
                return (a + b) / 2.0;
            }

            std::string format_result(double val) {
                return "Result: " + std::to_string(val);
            }

            int main() {
                int x = 90, y = 85;
                double avg = compute_average(x, y);

                int output = format_result(avg);

                std::cout << output << std::endl;
                return 0;
            }